  },
  "ingredients": [
    "8 slice bacon (chopped)",
    "800 gram ground beef",
    "1/4 cup cheddar cheese",
    "2 tablespoon fresh chives (chopped)",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "2 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1 tablespoon soy sauce (or coconut aminos)",
    "1 1/4 teaspoon salt",
    "1 teaspoon onion powder",
    "1 teaspoon worcestershire sauce"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "In a cast iron skillet, start cooking the slices of chopped bacon. You can season with spices if you’d like.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/IMG_4833.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue cooking it, covering the pan with a grease catcher – this stuff will get seriously messy without one!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/IMG_4838.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the bacon is cooked, remove it from the pan and set aside on some paper towels to crisp up.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/IMG_4842.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a large mixing bowl, add the ground beef.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/IMG_4847.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add 2/3 of your bacon, chopped chives, minced garlic, black pepper, soy sauce, salt, onion powder, and Worcestershire sauce.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/IMG_4851.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the meat and spice mixture together well; make sure that all of the spices are evenly distributed in the meat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/IMG_4856.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Form patties with your hands. You should be able to get relatively large patties from this.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/IMG_4858.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a cast iron skillet, add the previously saved bacon fat. Wait until it gets hot and then add your burger patties. You can add 3-4 at a time.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/IMG_4859.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Flip the burger patties after 3-5 minutes (depending on the done-ness you want) and continue to cook on the other side.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/IMG_4861.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve with cheese, extra bacon, and onion if you’d like. Also, feel free to add a dash of sriracha over the top!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/inside-out-bacon-burger/#wprm-recipe-50917-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/baconburger3.jpg"
    }
  ],
